- **Each layer imports only what this table allows, besides itself.** `rotproof check` reads the imports and fails on
  any other, and on an import of a layer or level declared in `absent`, which the table allows but the project does
  not have. Only direct imports are judged: what the table allows is closed under chaining. Imports built at run
  time are not seen. Each layer's role is in the documentation `rotproof create` wrote into it.
